Z||000000||Cliff Pennock||09-22-2001||06:11 PM||||I just received this by email. It's from a search engine that supposedly is doing something "good". Is it me, or are some people trying to make money out of the recent events? I've changed the name of the search engine for obvious reasons.<P><FONT COLOR="red">Dear Cliff,<P>Like many, companies and citizens alike, we are all searching for a way to help in light of last week’s tragedy. For Webmasters around the world wondering how they can participate in America's recovery, ************ is offering a simple way to help. In recognition of the heroism and loss of rescue workers, ************ will donate 10% of its earnings from Keyword Advertising for the remainder of September to the New York Chapter of the International Association of Firefighters (IAFF), the rescue department hardest hit by last Tuesday's disasters with more than 300 firefighters still missing.<P>Any deposit made into your Keyword Advertising account during September will generate a donation to the IAFF on your behalf.<P>Current customers: To log in to your Keyword Advertising account and make a deposit, click here: <A HREF="http://www.************.com/login" TARGET=_blank>http://www.************.com/login</A> <P>New Customers: To open a new account to bid on your Web site's keywords, click here: <A HREF="http://bidding.************.com" TARGET=_blank>http://bidding.************.com</A> <BR>Please log in with this User Name: ************<P>We wanted to find a way to help our nation recover. We hope this small gesture offers our Webmasters around the world a way to fight back and is a visible demonstration of our company's commitment to help our nation rebuild.<P>Sincerely,<BR>************<BR></FONT><P>First of all, I'm not a customer of this search engine, so they are trying to get my business through this. Seconds, they are willing to donate a whopping <B>10%</B> of their earnings till the end of September??? That's 7 days?<P>What say I don't give these ***holes any of my money and donate directly?<P>Maybe I'm seeing this all wrong, but stuff like this pi**** me off tremendously.||||reg||8
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||09-22-2001||06:45 PM||||I agree.. The spammers are going to have a great time with the subject liners now because of the stuff going on lately..<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||09-22-2001||06:47 PM||||I personally don't go for any company or business doing that. Giving 10% of earnings is   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">  !!<BR>If you want to give to a specific charity or fund I believe it's better to go straight to the source. Having your customers front the money so your company gets credit is a load of "carp". Here in Chicago the local newspaper is accepting money/donations for the fireman and rescuers. Your name is supplied as a contributor and they are not taking any of the funds received as "operating/business/administration fee" like most do. All 100% of the money goes straight to the funds listed. Many charities take out "administrative costs" But the local newspaper is donating their time. This is great that they are doing it this way. At least you know that ALL the money goes to those that are doing the work or need it and they have your name as a contributor.<BR>It is always upsetting where places like the Crusade of Mercy took over 50% of the money as administrative costs. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||09-22-2001||07:05 PM||||They're just looking to expand their customer base.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-22-2001||07:54 PM||||I urge everyone to boycot any company using the WTC disaster as a marketting tool.<P>For those in the Delaware Valley, one such Company is Eagle Limo. They've been running a radio spot for their long haul rides that plays on peoples current nags about flying and ends something to the effect, the world is sad but you can feel safe with Eagle Limo...<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Brian87egotrip||09-22-2001||09:28 PM||||That's just a damn shame. People should boycott companies doing that. I know I will. <P>------------------<BR>Brian                    87GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||sloth85GT||09-22-2001||10:30 PM||||you should say what search engine it is, that way we all can do something about it.<P>I personally like what McDonalds is doing, they have those McDonals Childrens Charity's boxes in front of the till that people can put money in and stuff, that way people give whatever they want, directly to the cause. My gf works as a Manager at McDonals and she told me that daily it's about $5 with the Childrens Charity's thing, and last night, it was $12. Now her McD's is REALLY slow, so if you look at the whole of that, the REALLY busy McD's are pulling in big bucks for the cause. And I think that's fantastic.<p>[This message has been edited by sloth85GT (edited 09-22-2001).]||||reg||1
